uild on each, and bails out immediately with nil and the error if any single call fails, otherwise collecting all results into a slice.\n\nI'm tracing through the test cases: running three inputs where all succeed should return the three values in order, while running a set that includes a broken input should return nil and the error, confirming atomic failure semantics.\n\nFor cmd/planner/main.go, I need the output to be newline-terminated with a non-zero exit code on error. I'm writing a main function that reads stdin, calls plan.Build, and either prints the error to stderr and exits with code 1, or prints the result with a trailing newline.\n\nNow I'm checking the Cache struct - it currently has a `last string` field, and I'm considering whether to add a `lastInput []byte` field alongside it since the tests only construct it with `&Cache{}` without setting fields directly, so adding a field shouldn't break anything. I'm also re-examining the graph ordering test, which builds a small graph with nodes \"a\" and \"b\" and loops twenty times checking consistency of the returned order.\n\nThe test also checks that a self-referencing node triggers a cycle error, which my implementation should already catch. Moving to the plan test, I'm looking at how it builds a dependency structure from JSON input with \"app\" depending on \"lib\".\n\nAdding validation test cases...\n\nThe test also checks that the cycle case exits with non-zero status, confirming println adds the newline and os.Exit(1) handles the error path correctly. Now I'll implement all the fixes.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":877,"cache_read_input_tokens":17997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":877},"output_tokens":12,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessio